dim]On an open task that lives in an inbox note, every Ctrl+Shift+P [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Task Card commit and every Ctrl+Shift+Enter toggle first asks where[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the task goes. Nothing is written until a destination is chosen. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]The task then lands in its new home with the action applied, and a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]review-walk landing advances to the next item, so morning triage [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never needs a separate Ctrl+Shift+M.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]inbox_routing.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/inbox_routing.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-4q[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-4q/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Inbox routing core in bob-navigation-hotkeys[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]route-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]route-core: add the inbox-note classifier, the route picker modal, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preflight, the routed move commit (no focus, no park), the walk's new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`route` outcome kind, and the nav api `inboxRoute` v1 namespace, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unit and runtime tests; nav 2.9.0.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Route gate on Ctrl+Shift+P Task Card commits[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]task-card-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after route-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-card-gate: route every non-closing single and counted Task Card [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit on an inbox task through one picker gate (prompt, write, move, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]settle the walk once), show the Inbox header chip, and add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]action-by-action conformance matrix; nav 2.10.0.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Route gate on Ctrl+Shift+Enter in block-id-prompt[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]link-toggle-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after route-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]link-toggle-gate: have block-id-prompt's link and unlink paths ask [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through nav `inboxRoute` before writing, move after a committed toggle, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and compose one toast with a `route` walk outcome. Fall back to today's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior when nav lacks the api; block-id-prompt 1.23.0.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs, rollout log, and decision-record follow-up[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-and-rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after task-card-gate, link-toggle-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-and-rollout: document inbox routing in bob-cli docs (projects, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness ritual and rollout log, getting-started, nav api §9), run the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]full plugin suite, deploy, and file a memory bead for a decisions [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strand.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-4q","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-4q.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a746c135b9cd12b05723435a35b9863a","started_at":"2026-10-06T19:02:18.611802+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"mis